SSB Microphone Gain

Space opens ALC preparation. Switch speech processing off for basic adjustment. At Continue Y/N?, y starts monitoring; n or q cancels preparation. After speaking, release PTT to hear sampled peak ALC. Brief peaks may be missed; raw units are not calibrated percentages or an audio-quality verdict. Space then clears the peak. A required meter selection is restored on exit while receiving; failures are reported. Restore your own preparation settings.

With PTT released, full stop increases gain; comma decreases it. Values stop at the ends. h reads this help; q returns to Settings with Done, keeping gain; v reads gain. Opening changes nothing. A mode change ends adjustment; reopen the control. YAC never starts transmission.

Before transmitting, connect a suitable antenna or dummy load and set suitable power yourself. Lower power does not make an unsuitable load safe. Use physical PTT and speak normally.

